{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-splade-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-1_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The last two types of coffee beans are Liberica and Excelsa. Liberica beans have nearly twice the caffeine of Arabica beans, which is a significant amount. Excelsa beans, on the other hand, have a similar caffeine content to Robusta beans, which is less than Liberica. In terms of shape, Liberica beans are known to be larger and more elongated than other coffee beans, while Excelsa beans are smaller and more rounded. This difference in shape can affect the way the beans are processed and roasted, which in turn can impact the flavor and aroma of the final product. Overall, Liberica beans tend to have a more robust and full-bodied flavor, while Excelsa beans are known for their fruity and complex character.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 26.36859130859375, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:9": 25.096426010131836, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:8": 23.97737693786621, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:12": 23.757699966430664, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:4": 23.698225021362305}, "ptkb_provenance": ["Excelsa has recently been reclassified as a type of Liberica coffee because it thrives in the same conditions and grows a similarly tall tree. But the actual coffee it produces is vastly different. It has a much fruitier character than Liberica, with a tart acidity that makes it popular for adding complexity to coffee blends. Excelsa coffee makes up only about 7% of the current coffee market. Still, given its appealing flavor profile and the fact that it is nearly as resilient and productive as Robusta, this seems likely to grow. Much like Robusta, Excelsa coffee has been regarded as poor quality, but this is more due to poor growing and processing practices than the bean itself. With the proper care, Excelsa has the potential to be specialty-grade coffee.", "Liberica beans make up only about 2% of the world's current coffee crop. Once upon a time, this varietal was far more critical after disease wiped out much of the world's Arabica supply. Arabica has since made a comeback, and Liberica production has primarily ceased. However, that may change in the future, as climate change makes it increasingly challenging to produce the more sensitive Arabica plants reliably. Liberica coffee has a unique flavor, pairing floral and fruity notes with a deep smokiness that some describe as woody. It has a full-bodied, reminiscent of Robusta coffee. It's not to everyone's taste, but there are some exceptional Liberica coffees to be had when done right."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:6": 26.36859130859375, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:9": 25.096426010131836, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:8": 23.97737693786621, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:12": 23.757699966430664, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:4": 23.698225021362305, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:5": 23.57366180419922, "clueweb22-en0031-16-17635:8": 23.275739669799805, "clueweb22-en0001-37-16016:10": 23.191560745239258, "clueweb22-en0020-47-18754:2": 22.94225311279297, "clueweb22-en0001-20-10010:19": 22.79440689086914, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:7": 22.621318817138672, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:13": 22.50435447692871, "clueweb22-en0011-55-07210:14": 22.295358657836914, "clueweb22-en0006-97-10057:5": 22.009471893310547, "clueweb22-en0019-88-13848:4": 21.90607261657715, "clueweb22-en0031-65-00073:17": 21.874618530273438, "clueweb22-en0019-88-13848:5": 21.7800235748291, "clueweb22-en0035-25-05669:9": 21.2956600189209, "clueweb22-en0022-85-00226:7": 21.20197296142578, "clueweb22-en0036-21-16351:3": 21.040891647338867, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:4": 20.614547729492188, "clueweb22-en0001-20-10010:18": 20.42721939086914, "clueweb22-en0045-33-05805:1": 20.317729949951172, "clueweb22-en0029-40-16358:6": 20.259746551513672, "clueweb22-en0004-97-11464:5": 20.21397590637207, "clueweb22-en0030-14-16395:14": 20.191267013549805, "clueweb22-en0043-72-19569:4": 20.181