{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-splade-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Congratulations on your pregnancy! You're probably thinking about how to prepare for breastfeeding. First, know that breastfeeding is not bad for you or your baby. In fact, it's strongly recommended by health experts due to its many health benefits. You'll want to eat a well-balanced diet while breastfeeding, including a variety of fruits, vegetables, starchy foods, protein, and dairy. Drinking plenty of water is also essential, aiming for 12 glasses a day. You can also consider lactation drinks to help stay hydrated and produce more breast milk. However, be aware that a low-carb diet can be dangerous for breastfeeding moms. Additionally, alcohol can interfere with milk supply, so it's best to limit or avoid it altogether. If you're concerned about running out of milk, try fitting in extra breastfeeds each day. Your breasts will get the message to make more milk each time your baby nurses. With the right information, support, and care, most mothers can breastfeed and produce enough", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0030-81-08172:4": 19.098058700561523, "clueweb22-en0012-14-02860:4": 18.782907485961914, "clueweb22-en0032-68-05574:6": 18.257957458496094, "clueweb22-en0016-79-13986:0": 18.11223602294922, "clueweb22-en0013-94-16728:6": 18.05828285217285}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I think I don't get enough calcium, and I am worried about it.", "I am a woman.", "I like eating cake as a snack with coffee, and I bake cakes every week.", "Sometimes I drink fresh orange juice in the afternoon.", "I eat jam for breakfast.", "I prefer foods with more nutrients and protein.", "I am interested in low-carb food."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0030-81-08172:4": 19.098058700561523, "clueweb22-en0012-14-02860:4": 18.782907485961914, "clueweb22-en0032-68-05574:6": 18.257957458496094, "clueweb22-en0016-79-13986:0": 18.11223602294922, "cluew