{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-splade-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Fractional CO2 laser treatment is a less invasive version of the traditional CO2 laser treatment. It targets only a fraction of the skin's surface, leaving the surrounding skin intact. This results in less downtime and less discomfort compared to the fully ablative CO2 laser treatment. Fractional treatments can be repeated more frequently, and they're often used to treat smaller areas of the skin. On the other hand, fully ablative CO2 laser treatment is a more intense procedure that removes the top layer of skin, revealing smoother, fresher skin beneath. It's often used to treat more extensive skin concerns, such as deep wrinkles, scars, and sun damage. However, it requires more downtime and may involve general anesthesia. Choose the one that suits your skin concerns and desired level of invasiveness. If you're looking for a faster recovery and less discomfort, fractional CO2 laser treatment might be the better option for you. If you're willing to invest in a more intense treatment with longer downtime,", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:12": 37.239479064941406, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:11": 33.84709548950195, "clueweb22-en0009-27-04860:6": 33.68170166015625, "clueweb22-en0016-80-15701:9": 33.67998504638672, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:9": 33.62217712402344}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I usually wear makeup to even out my complexion.", "I'm interested in treatments that improve my skin with minimal downtime."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:12": 37.239479064941406, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:11": 33.84709548950195, "clueweb22-en0009-27-04860:6": 33.68170166015625, "clueweb22-en0016-80-15701:9": 33.67998504638672, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:9": 33.62217712402344, "clueweb22-en0009-27-04860:7": 33.55