{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-splade-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "When checking a second-hand bike, start by making sure the wheels aren't bent and that the seat and rear frame are properly aligned with the rest of the bike. You should also check that the front part, especially the headlight, is pointing straight. If anything looks misaligned, like the steering or rear wheel being off by a centimeter or so, it's best to get it repaired or replaced safely. Used bikes can also have issues with the swingarm, so it's good to be cautious there too. If you're unsure, a mechanic can do a full check-up and give you a written report confirming everything is in good shape. That might be a good option for you, especially since you mentioned you're not very handy with DIY. For your comfort, consider a gel bike seat or a gel cushion adds-on seat. Also, think about the handlebar setup, the right width, rise, and sweep can improve posture, reduce wrist strain, and make technical terrain easier to handle", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0043-13-03064:3": 28.506786346435547, "clueweb22-en0025-76-12903:3": 28.22391700744629, "clueweb22-en0025-76-12903:2": 28.075531005859375, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:8": 27.421005249023438, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:7": 27.09109115600586}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I have a small garage that I use as workshop space at home.", "I value comfort over speed.", "I'm a casual bike rider.", "I am not really handy with DIY.", "I recently moved to a city with more hills and rough paths.", "I take my bike in the train and the bus.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0043-13-03064:3": 28.506786346435547, "clueweb22-en0025-76-12903:3": 28.22391700744629, "clueweb22-en0025-76-12903:2": 28.075531005859375, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:8": 27.421005249023438, "clueweb22-en0002-05-13020:7": 27.09109115600586, "clueweb22-en0023-24-200